# CODEOWNERS — paired with `require_code_owner_reviews` on the `main`
# branch-protection rule. GitHub resolves this file by walking the
# repository from the changed file up to the root and taking the **last**
# matching pattern, so order matters: put more-specific patterns after
# less-specific ones. A reviewer approval from any listed owner satisfies
# the rule for a PR.
#
# Single-owner project today: every path defaults to @greysquirr3l. The
# security-critical sections below repeat @greysquirr3l explicitly so
# future reviewers see them highlighted in the PR Owners panel rather
# than collapsing into the default fallback line, and so that splitting a
# path out into its own rule later is a one-line edit instead of a hunt.

# Default — every path is owned by the project owner.
/*    @greysquirr3l

# Security-critical surface — release pipeline, SBOM, branch protection
# automation, signing, and security policy. Reviewed by @greysquirr3l
# (same owner today; this block exists so the rule is explicit and
# greppable if a second owner is ever added for these areas).
/.github/workflows/release.yml           @greysquirr3l
/.github/workflows/scorecard.yml         @greysquirr3l
/.github/dependabot.yml                  @greysquirr3l
/.github/CODEOWNERS                      @greysquirr3l
/docs/security-audit.md                  @greysquirr3l
/SECURITY.md                             @greysquirr3l

# Cryptographic / supply-chain configuration — Rust toolchain pin, deny
# license/advisory policy, and Cargo's own lockfile.
/rust-toolchain.toml                     @greysquirr3l
/deny.toml                               @greysquirr3l
/Cargo.lock                              @greysquirr3l
